{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5uwn6WEpUDPoy8Hdcf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the format in the `DurationField` error message. In `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py:1590` it now reads `[DD] [[HH:]MM:]ss[.uuuuuu]` instead of `[DD] [HH:[MM:]]ss[.uuuuuu]`. That matches how durations are actually parsed: \"14:00\" means 14 minutes, so seconds are required, minutes are optional, and hours can only be given if minutes are.\n\nI ran the `model_fields` tests: 260 pass and 1 fails. The failure is `model_fields.test_durationfield.TestValidation.test_invalid_string`, which still checks for the old message text word for word. That test needs the new format string, but I didn't edit it because the rules don't allow changing test files.\n\nThere are two things I deliberately didn't do:\n- **Translations:** the `.po` files under `django/conf/locale/` still contain the old string. Translators update those, so I didn't edit them by hand.\n- **Default `help_text`:** the issue also suggests giving duration fields a default `help_text` showing the format. I left that out to keep the fix minimal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":609,"cache_read_input_tokens":27485,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":609},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dc13ead-3ca3-4def-908c-d41c023bb514","uuid":"2edf0c9b-2068-4399-8a27-3379554c9b1b","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:39:32.744Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5uwduwXHLuLfEaQxeW"}
